    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88), who stands as our premier start. His matchup against Arrighetti is bolstered by an elite 16% SP skill advantage and a \"Slow SP Delivery\" tag, which significantly enhances his stolen base probability\u2014a critical factor given our strategic emphasis on speed. **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) follow closely, both benefiting from a favorable 4.46\u20134.99 xERA range for their respective opponents and a substantial 10% park factor bump. **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) also earns a high-tier start, as his 19% SP skill advantage against the RHP makes him a must-play despite the standard lineup rotation.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Josh Jung** (41.87), who sits just shy of our \"Strong\" tier. While he remains a core component of our long-term strategy, the combination of facing an elite arm like Murphy (2.70 xERA) and the superior efficiency ratings of **Miguel Vargas** (63.06) pushed him out of the starting nine. **Heliot Ramos** (44.20) represents our most volatile start; he enters the lineup on the strength of our 5x5 Roto needs, but his sub-45 score serves as a warning that he is riding the edge of our efficiency floor due to a challenging matchup against Woo.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical risks today, primarily the sub-optimal outlook for **Heliot Ramos**, whose projection is suppressed by a 5% park penalty. Furthermore, **Drake Baldwin** (58.04) faces a tough left-handed matchup against Gore, which keeps him in the \"Marginal\" category. Should the official lineups confirm any shifts, specifically regarding the leadoff spots for **Sam Antonacci** or **Jacob Wilson**, we may reassess, but for now, the data confirms a focused attack on the mid-tier xERA arms in today\u2019s slate to maximize our counting stats.",
